WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.510
Imagine a couple blessed with twin babies
who are conjoint.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.550
Now if they are to be
separated, then one of them is sure to lose

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.010
life.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:19.630
But raising the conjoined twins is
not only difficult for the parents, but even

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.090
for the kids themselves!

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.340
So what
should be done in this case?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.060
These questions give us goosebumps!

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.200
But they are always a part of the medical
field.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.239
And how are the answers to such traumatising
questions found?

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:40.100
Well, although we cannot really answer such
questions completely, but still to

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.910
reach the best conclusion, we have the concept
of BIOETHICS coming to our

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.000
rescue!

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.160
In the previous videos we learned about the
Transgenic organisms which are

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.040
produced and used for human benefit.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.280
But the production of transgenic animals
comes at the cost of disturbing the natural

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.989
genome of those organisms.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.740
So do you
think this is morally correct?

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.490
You may say no!

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.930
We should not use organisms for
our selfish motto!

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:15.990
Okay… so how do we test the newer medicines?

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.990
As the disease
or disorder intensity is increasing exponentially,

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:24.900
so is the need for newer and
more efficient medicines!

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.370
So if there are no model organisms, then testing
medicines will not be possible.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:34.460
So how will new medicines be discovered and
used?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.290
That indicates the need of using model organisms!

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.590
So what should be done ideally?

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.340
There is no single answer for this actually.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.240
And
hence, for these types of concerns we have

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.090
the field of bioethics.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.810
Now let us first understand what Bioethics
is!

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.350
It is simply the area dealing with
ethical issues in the field of Medicine or

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.500
any other biological studies.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.700
In this video, let us learn about bioethics
in the field of biotechnology.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.340
Let us begin with the same point that we discussed
a few minutes

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.560
back...Transgenic organisms!

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.670
Genetic engineering enables us to study the
various genetic disorders.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.700
And for
these types of studies, transgenic animal

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.121
models, like the Transgenic mice are
developed.

00:02:24.121 --> 00:02:26.120
Transgenic animal models are Developed for
Particular genetic disorder

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:32.790
These animals, as we know are called Genetically
Modified Organisms or GMOs.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.650
And just like animals, plants are also modified.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:42.040
So the transgenic crops produced
also have qualities that we desire!

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.540
Just like the Golden rice for example!

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.379
It
contains wholesome amount of Beta-carotene,

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:52.830
which is the precursor of Vitamin
A. When consumed, the compound gets converted

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.930
to Vitamin A in the body.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.050
Thus,
the transgenic rice variety is a boon to areas

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:02.409
hit with Vitamin A deficiency.

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:07.239
But if the organisms are so beneficial to
us, then is their production really an

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.220
ethical concern?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.670
Yes!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.900
That is the other side of the coin!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:18.830
GMOs are known to produce several
compounds, among which, a few can be toxic

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.650
or allergenic in nature.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.849
We cannot ensure that these untraced compounds
would not harm us.

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:28.629
Thus,
there are several hidden risks attached to

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:29.629
this.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:34.650
There can be possibilities that the
GMOs turn out to be actually more harmful

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.400
rather than being beneficial.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.590
The long
term side effects of GMOs are still unknown.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:47.769
Also, as we know that transgenic organisms
have a completely different gene pool

00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:50.780
from the wild varieties.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:54.310
So at the species level, we disturb the genetic
composition

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.599
of those organisms!

00:03:55.599 --> 00:03:59.849
Do we really know what impact this can create
several years

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:01.480
later?

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:06.830
What can happen if the transgenic genes sustain
in the gene pool forever?

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.090
And what if natural genes are lost?

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:14.970
There are many other questions that emerge
as we go deeper in this discussion!

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.900
Hence, making “transgenic organisms” is
an ethical concern!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.430
So what is the
solution to this?

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.740
There is no fixed solution for this, but yes,
there are few

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.020
regulatory bodies which glance at the various
activities in the field of

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.440
biotechnology.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:38.590
Now let us talk about one more hot topic in
bioethics...that is Cloning!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:43.310
We know that cloning in biotechnology deals
with the process of making exact

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:48.090
copies of biomolecules or organisms.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.460
How about Human cloning?

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.490
The idea sounds cool!

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.389
But that is not so great in
reality!

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:59.750
Preparing human clones without regulation
would definitely lead to

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.160
serious concerns, like overpopulation, increase
in diseases, exhaustion of limited

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.630
resources and many more!

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:12.120
Also, this can act against the balance of
nature.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.560
We
know that nature promotes variation in gene

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.250
pool of organisms.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:21.220
Cloning can lead
to utilisation of the same gene pool constantly,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.340
thus leading to a loss of vigour in
the genes.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:29.680
And there are many other issues which pop
up with the process of making clones!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:36.820
Thus, the question whether cloning is favourable
or not still remains unanswered!

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.540
For all such questions, which literally churn
our minds, the only option that comes

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.120
to our rescue is Bioethics!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.919
There are several rules and regulatory laws
laid under

00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:53.540
bioethics, that help us make wise decisions
as we stumble upon heart wrenching

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.509
obstacles!

